      "problem": "Factor ${x}^{4}-{x}^{2}-6.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $z={x}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}-6 & ={({x}^{2})}^{2}-({x}^{2})-6 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-z-6 & =(z+2)(z-3) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2)({x}^{2}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
